  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-13 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Hotel, Resort, and Hospitality Management - Lodging Management Emphasis program page (poid=10968) and its linked official degree map, 'Hotel, Resort, & Hospitality Management Degree Maps (2026-2027)', tab 'Lodging (Campus)' (the workbook's Index lists Online as N/A for this emphasis), last updated/reviewed July 27, 2026. Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. Collected as the BS: the program is a combined BA/BS, the catalog prints a single combined Total Credits, BA/BS Degree: 120, and the map expressly states that students electing the BA take 16 credits of one foreign language, which are not included in the map; the BS version is recorded, following the prior-wave pattern for combined BA/BS programs. Every semester's courses sum to the map's printed semester total (15/16/15/15/15/15/14/15) and the plan to the catalog's printed Total Credits, BA/BS Degree: 120. Per the catalog, students must complete the courses required for the major with a GPA of 2.5 or better. The catalog's HRHM Core Requirements (52 credits) are exercised exactly by the map: every named core course is placed (ACCT 2010, BA 1010, ECON 2020, HRHM 2000, HRHM 3010, HRHM 3020, HRHM 3110, HRHM 3300, HRHM 3400, HRHM 3510, HRHM 3610, HRHM 4200, HRHM 4400, HRHM 4500 at 1 credit, MGMT 2000, MGMT 4100, MKTG 3010 and NFS 1020). The Lodging Management Emphasis Requirements are headed 9 credits in the catalog and are exercised by the map as HRHM 4700 at 3 credits in Fall Year 3 and HRHM 4110 and HRHM 4300 in Spring Year 4, completing the catalog's Curriculum of 61 credits. DISCLOSED catalog range, not reconciled: the catalog lists HRHM 4700 Special Topics in Hospitality Management at 3-6 credits (or an approved HRHM elective, including study abroad), so the emphasis items as printed sum to 9-12 credits; the map places HRHM 4700 at 3 credits, the value recorded here, which is the value at which the block sums to its printed 9 credits. The map's free-elective rows total 37 credits as printed (3/6/6/6/6/4/6); the catalog prints no free-elective figure. Catalog course titles are recorded where the map shortens them.",
